description:
Start a flag release: release a flag across environments by a flag release plan (kind "plan") or a list of environments (kind "custom"). When the user names no project, call get-projects before you ask anything. In an interactive run, confirm the project, the flag, and the plan or each environment's release with the user before you send confirm: true. When you picked the project because the user named none, name it and wait for their reply first. With kind "plan", flagReleasePlanKey names the plan (from get-flag-release-plans; default: true unless the user picks another). Prefer kind "custom" when the project has no flag release plan or none fits the request; otherwise use a plan. With kind "custom", environments lists each environment in release order, as in create-automated-rollout-config. An immediate environment is only environmentKey (releaseType is never immediate). A multi-variate flag needs startingVariationId and endingVariationId (variation _ids); a boolean flag omits both (false to true). Send pullRequest (repoFullName as owner/name, and number) for a pull request's release. A webhook environment then waits for a deploy that includes the merge. Without a pull request, it starts on the next deploy signal for that environment. Returns config_id and the release as read back; manage it with the *-automated-rollout-config tools. Report all returned warnings; an environment with one is not a clean release.
Examples:
- plan, boolean flag, no pull request: {"projectKey":"default","flagKey":"new-checkout","flagReleasePlanKey":"standard","confirm":true}
- plan, multi-variate flag: {"projectKey":"default","flagKey":"theme","flagReleasePlanKey":"standard","startingVariationId":"<from _id>","endingVariationId":"<to _id>","confirm":true}
- custom, staging immediate, then production by its default release plan: {"projectKey":"default","flagKey":"new-checkout","environments":[{"environmentKey":"staging"},{"environmentKey":"production","releaseType":"policy"}],"confirm":true}

environments.description:
Only with kind custom, and required there: each environment, in release order. One example entry per release type. Omit triggerType unless the user says when the release starts.
- immediate: {"environmentKey":"production"}
- progressive: {"environmentKey":"production","releaseType":"override","override":{"releaseMethod":"progressive","rolloutContextKindKey":"user","stages":[{"allocation":10000,"durationMillis":3600000},{"allocation":100000,"durationMillis":3600000}]}}
- guarded: {"environmentKey":"production","releaseType":"override","override":{"releaseMethod":"guarded","rolloutContextKindKey":"user","stages":[{"allocation":10000,"durationMillis":3600000}],"metricKeys":["error-rate"],"rollbackOnRegression":true}}
- policy with a named environment release plan, which always needs releaseType policy: {"environmentKey":"production","releaseType":"policy","environmentReleasePlanKey":"prod-ramp"}
